
log PCaco fits                            11/12/02

I have redone the MC/LR calculations for the 50
B-I Yazdanian compounds using 725 waters and averaging for
20M configurations. This is the xLR725CMA script with the
BOSS Windows version. The fits are basically the same as before.
The only 2 descriptors that matter are the saturated amine count
(#amine) and a FISA term. Labetalol is the only outlier that I exclude
and I don't do methyl scopolamine since it is a quaternary ammonium
species. For the remaining 49 compounds, the fit results
including the intercept, #amine and the following are:

                r^2      rms
FISA           0.678    0.434
FISA/glob      0.709    0.412
FISA/glob^2    0.724    0.401
FISA/glob^3    0.721    0.403

So, the FISA/glob^2 term still wins, though these fits are all
pretty equivalent.

We'll redo the Affymax compounds now and make an official combined fit.
